on FreeBSD and Linux: location /video/ {
aio            on;
output_buffers 1 64k;
} On FreeBSD, AIO can be used starting from FreeBSD 4.3.
Prior to FreeBSD 11.0,
AIO can either be linked statically into a kernel: options VFS_AIO or loaded dynamically as a kernel loadable module: kldload aio On Linux, AIO can be used starting from kernel version 2.6.22.
Also, it is necessary to enable directio ,
or otherwise reading will be blocking: location /video/ {
aio            on;
directio       512;
output_buffers 1 128k;
} On Linux, directio can only be used for reading blocks that are aligned on 512-byte
boundaries (or 4K for XFS).
